> Converted from personal notes. Amounts are for one serving. Directions are editorial, not verified source instructions.

> REVIEW: Gia's dough formula remains missing; prepared GF crust is the active alternative.

== Ingredients ==

Gather the following ingredients: @gluten-free pizza crusts (10-12 in){2/5} (prepared), @gluten-free pizza sauce{1/5%cup}, @low-moisture mozzarella{12/5%oz} (shredded), @olive oil{2/5%tbsp}, @dried oregano{1/5%tsp}, @fresh basil{1/20%cup}, @?bell pepper{1/5} (sliced), @?mushrooms{8/5%oz} (sliced), @?gluten-free pepperoni{4/5%oz}.

== Preparation ==

Prepare the gluten-free crust according to package or linked source instructions.

Add sauce, cheese and toppings; bake until the crust is cooked and cheese is bubbling.
